  <metadata>
    <name>Boawae to Nangaroro direct</name>
    <desc>Boawae to Nangaroro direct (alternative): Skip Mbay and the Aesesa plain: cross from Boawae straight over to the south coast at Nangaroro. Shorter and less remote; a bad-weather or time-limit fallback. 48.8 km, +1151 m. Replaces 117.9 km / +2284 m of the main course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:59Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.766700" lon="121.164400">
    <ele>500.7</ele>
    <name>Boawae</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: town | resupply: basic | water: reliable | sleep: homestay -- Main south-central town of Nagekeo Regency, on the northwest slope of Ebulobo volcano, on the Trans-Flores highway. Position corrected ~13.0 km to the Kantor Camat Boawae / Polsek Boawae cluster (Overture Maps place them</desc>
    <sym>City (Medium)</sym>
    <type>anchor/town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.786389" lon="121.391667">
    <ele>19.0</ele>
    <name>Nangaroro</name>
    <desc>km 48.8 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- South-coast district of Nagekeo Regency bordering Ende; farming and fishing villages (Tonggo etc.), grey-stone beaches; an alternative south-coast crossing from Boawae/Mbay toward Ende.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.816667" lon="121.192333">
    <ele>2105.8</ele>
    <name>Ebulobo</name>
    <desc>[highlight] An active stratovolcano (2,124-2,137 m) above Boawae in southern Nagekeo Regency; first recorded eruption 1830, most recent in the 1980s-2000s.</desc>
    <sym>Summit</sym>
    <type>poi/volcano</type>
  </wpt>
